{"causes": ["The Ottoman Empire's aggressive expansion into the Balkans in the early 15th century created an existential threat to independent Albanian principalities.", "Skanderbeg's upbringing as an Ottoman hostage and his military training within their Janissary corps provided him invaluable insight into their strategies and weaknesses.", "The fragmented political landscape of Albania, characterized by independent feudal lords, necessitated a unifying figure to effectively counter the centralized Ottoman power."], "effects": ["Skanderbeg's resistance delayed the Ottoman conquest of Albania by over two decades, significantly impacting their timeline for further European expansion.", "His military victories against the Ottoman Empire provided a critical moral boost to Christian Europe and influenced anti-Ottoman alliances and crusading efforts.", "Skanderbeg became an enduring symbol of Albanian national identity and resistance, profoundly shaping the country's historical consciousness and cultural heritage."], "relationships": [{"sourceSlug": "ottoman-empire", "sourceName": "Ottoman Empire", "verb": "CAUSES", "targetSlug": "skanderbeg", "targetName": "Skanderbeg", "context": "The relentless expansion of the Ottoman Empire into the Balkans directly caused Skanderbeg to abandon his service to them and lead an Albanian resistance from 1443."}, {"sourceSlug": "skanderbeg", "sourceName": "Skanderbeg", "verb": "PARTICIPATES_IN", "targetSlug": "ottoman-albanian-wars", "targetName": "Ottoman-Albanian Wars", "context": "Skanderbeg was the preeminent military leader of the Albanian forces throughout the Ottoman-Albanian Wars, leading the League of Lezhë from 1444 until his death in 1468."}, {"sourceSlug": "league-of-lezhe", "sourceName": "League of Lezhë", "verb": "COLLABORATES_WITH", "targetSlug": "skanderbeg", "targetName": "Skanderbeg", "context": "Skanderbeg was the elected captain and primary commander of the League of Lezhë, a military and political alliance of Albanian principalities formed in 1444."}, {"sourceSlug": "skanderbeg", "sourceName": "Skanderbeg", "verb": "INFLUENCES", "targetSlug": "albanian-nationalism", "targetName": "Albanian Nationalism", "context": "Skanderbeg's struggle for independence against the Ottoman Empire profoundly influenced the development of Albanian national identity and nationalist movements centuries later."}, {"sourceSlug": "skanderbeg", "sourceName": "Skanderbeg", "verb": "OCCURS_IN", "targetSlug": "kruje-albania", "targetName": "Krujë, Albania", "context": "Skanderbeg's primary stronghold and capital was Krujë, which he successfully defended against multiple major Ottoman sieges throughout his campaigns."}], "places": [{"name": "Krujë, Albania", "role": "Capital and stronghold"}, {"name": "Lezhë, Albania", "role": "Formation of League"}, {"name": "Naples, Italy", "role": "Diplomatic ally"}], "texts": [{"title": "Wikipedia: Skanderbeg", "type": "Reference article", "slug": "skanderbeg"}], "externalLinks": ["https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q160614", "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Skanderbeg"], "tags": ["Political Leaders", "political-systems", "geopolitical-linkage", "cause-and-effect"], "thumbnailUrl": "", "quote": "", "legacySummary": "", "historicalSignificance": {"significanceScore": 7, "significanceNarrative": "Skanderbeg's two-decade resistance against the Ottoman Empire significantly delayed their advance into Western Europe, safeguarding the Italian peninsula for a critical period. His legacy became a foundational element of Albanian national identity and a potent symbol of defiance against overwhelming odds.", "significanceCategory": "regional"}, "_editLog": [{"timestamp": "2026-11-23T06:33:14Z", "editorId": "gemini-2.5-flash·cloud·GH#45123784585", "field": "summary", "oldValue": "Gjergj Kastrioti was an Albanian nobleman and military leader who led the League of Lezhë in the Ottoman-Albanian Wars until his death. Skanderbeg is considered to be a major figure of medieval Albanian history and today is the national hero of Albania.", "newValue": "Gjergj Kastrioti, universally known as Skanderbeg, was an Albanian nobleman and military commander who spearheaded a remarkably effective resistance against the expanding Ottoman Empire for over two decades in the mid-15th century (c. 1443–1468). Born into the Kastrioti principality in 1405, Skanderbeg’s strategic brilliance and unwavering resolve made him a pivotal figure in the defense of Christian Europe against Ottoman incursions, effectively delaying their advance into the Italian peninsula and establishing a profound, enduring legacy as Albania's national hero.

After being taken as a hostage by the Ottomans and serving in their military, Skanderbeg defected in 1443 during the Battle of Niš, returning to Albania to reclaim his ancestral lands. He united the Albanian principalities under the League of Lezhë in 1444, an unprecedented coalition that achieved significant victories against vastly superior Ottoman forces, notably at Torvioll (1444), Oronichea (1448), and Albulena (1457). His defense of Krujë, his stronghold, against multiple Ottoman sieges (most notably in 1450, 1466, and 1467) became legendary, demonstrating his mastery of mountain warfare and guerrilla tactics against Sultans Murad II and Mehmed II.

Skanderbeg's sustained resistance had profound consequences, preventing the Ottoman Empire from consolidating its control over the Balkan Peninsula and projecting power further west into Italy for a critical period. His diplomatic efforts forged alliances with the Kingdom of Naples, the Republic of Venice, and the Papacy, drawing wider European attention and support for the anti-Ottoman cause. Although Albania eventually fell to the Ottomans shortly after his death, Skanderbeg's struggle provided a powerful blueprint for national resistance and became a cornerstone of Albanian national identity and historical memory."}, {"timestamp": "2026-11-23T06:33:14Z", "editorId": "gemini-2.5-flash·cloud·GH#45123784585", "field": "detailsJson.causes", "oldValue": [{"title": "Medieval era: interplay of religious authority, feudal governance, and trade network expansion", "type": "EventWindow", "year": "1405-05-06, Sinë"}, {"title": "Political crises and power transitions requiring new leadership", "type": "Idea", "year": "1405-05-06, Sinë"}], "newValue": ["The Ottoman Empire's aggressive expansion into the Balkans in the early 15th century created an existential threat to independent Albanian principalities.", "Skanderbeg's upbringing as an Ottoman hostage and his military training within their Janissary corps provided him invaluable insight into their strategies and weaknesses.", "The fragmented political landscape of Albania, characterized by independent feudal lords, necessitated a unifying figure to effectively counter the centralized Ottoman power."]}, {"timestamp": "2026-11-23T06:33:14Z", "editorId": "gemini-2.5-flash·cloud·GH#45123784585", "field": "detailsJson.effects", "oldValue": [{"title": "Shaped political institutions and governance practices", "type": "Idea", "year": "1468-01-17"}, {"title": "Contributed to synthesis of classical and religious thought informing Renaissance and Reformati", "type": "Movement", "year": "1468-01-17"}], "newValue": ["Skanderbeg's resist